 The range window (`yamt --diff=<range>`, plan §2 #103–#107) has its own `RangeSource` (`RangeSource.ts`, read-only: `openRange`, `loadRangeFile`): the `RangeFileId` brand in `domain.ts`, camelCase shapes and their conversions in `rangeDomain.ts` (a texts reply's differences through `compareDomain.ts` `toDifferences`), the app's in `tauriRange.ts`, fixture mode's in `fixtureRange.ts` (`fixtures/range/<case>.json` = `{ start, files }`, a file's id its index; `?range` loads `review`, `?range=<case>` that case, an unknown case logs `range.fixture_miss` and lists nothing).
 
+`RangeStart` carries `heading` and `totals` as Rust computed them (request `docs/slices/request-mr-heading.md`, plan §2 proposed #199): `heading` is `typed`, `mergeRequest { iid, names: { title, source, target } }` or `unnamedMergeRequest { iid }`, `toRangeStart` brands `iid` naming `heading.iid`; `totals` is the listed files' counted lines summed, never recomputed here. Fixture mode's `?heading=mergeRequest|fork|hiddenFork|unnamed` replaces the shown case's heading only (its totals, sides and files stay, and the review fixtures see the replaced start); empty or absent keeps the case's, an unknown value logs `range.fixture_heading_miss` and keeps it.
+
 The range window's threads and GitLab (plan §2 #116–#120) come through `ReviewSource` (`ReviewSource.ts`: `listThreads`, `addThread`, `addNote`, `queueMessage`, `unqueueMessage`, `checkGitLab`, `sendQueue` and `sendMessage(message)` (plan §2 #198: the queue's send for that one message) with a progress callback over a `Channel`), which `RangeSource` extends: the `ThreadId`/`MessageId` brands in `domain.ts`, a thread's `ThreadPlace` in `threadLine.ts` (plan §2 #145–#148: `start` a `DiffLine` in GitLab's one-column order, `end` the `ThreadLine` whose column shows the box; `toThreadPlace` brands every number naming `….place.start.left`/`….place.end.right`, `fromThreadPlace` hands it back as is; `diffLineOf`, `onePlace`, `sameDiffLine`, `isOneLine`), camelCase shapes and their conversions in `reviewDomain.ts`, the app's in `tauriReview.ts`, fixture mode's in memory in `fixtureReview.ts` (`?threads=seeded`: one one-line thread of each line kind on the review case's `src/board/board.ts` with a queued, a refused, a pending and an `aiAnswer` message, then two range threads with a `notQueued` note each: unchanged 400/388 to added 405 and removed 254 to added 259; the store's refusals as Rust's: `EmptyMessage`, `UnknownRangeFile`, `UnknownThread`, `UnknownMessage`, `MessagePending`, `SendRunning`; each post after a 300 ms pause, progress per message; `sendMessage` is `sendQueue`'s path narrowed to that message: `SendRunning` first, then `UnknownMessage`, then the check, a message that does not wait `sent` 0 of 0 at once, and a script's outcome keyed by the message's place in the whole queue) over `fixtureGitLab.ts` (`?gitlab=<script>`: `linedUp` by default, `checking` answers after 3 s, one not-lined-up answer per script, `refusal` refuses and `stopped` times out at the second queued message; an unknown script logs `review.fixture_miss`).
 
